__pycache__/

# Job logs are per-run noise, but sbatch's --output=slurm_logs/%x-%j.out fails
# if the directory does not exist, so keep the directory itself in the clone.
slurm_logs/*
!slurm_logs/.gitkeep

# KAS caches. Most of dataset-cache/ is derived - NumpyKASVSLDataset.prepare()
# rewrites bucket*-indices.npy, instance-lengths.npy, bucketed-doc-indices-*.npy
# and dataset-metadata/metadata-*.npy from scratch - and at 64k docs it is
# ~1.4 GB per experiment. Ignore it by default.
experiments/*/dataset-cache/*

# One exception, for the tracked 1K sample datasets: dataset-metadata/train.csv is an INPUT, not
# a derived file. build_experiment_kas.py writes it from the 45 GB LMEnt shard
# and bucket_documents_kas() reads each document's entity token spans out of it
# (utils.py:452); without it prepare() cannot run and make_run_config.py rejects
# the experiment outright (make_run_config.py:33). It is not in the clone unless
# it is tracked, and it cannot be regenerated off-cluster.
#
# 22 MB each, ~3.2 MB packed. Do NOT extend this to larger corpora - the 64k-doc
# equivalent is ~1.4 GB and would be unrecoverable from history. Those get built
# on the cluster by build_experiment_kas.py and stay there.
!experiments/hollyday_clean_1000/dataset-cache/dataset-metadata/
experiments/hollyday_clean_1000/dataset-cache/dataset-metadata/*
!experiments/hollyday_clean_1000/dataset-cache/dataset-metadata/train.csv
!experiments/hollyday_1000_clean_10_poison/dataset-cache/dataset-metadata/
experiments/hollyday_1000_clean_10_poison/dataset-cache/dataset-metadata/*
!experiments/hollyday_1000_clean_10_poison/dataset-cache/dataset-metadata/train.csv


# Bulk corpus artifacts for larger sweep datasets. The two tracked 1K
# sample datasets are already tracked (1.4 MB of train.npy each) and .gitignore does
# not affect tracked files, so this only bites NEW experiments - where it must:
# at 64k documents train.npy is ~92 MiB, near GitHub's hard per-file limit, and
# the 45 GB shard needed to regenerate it is not in the repo. Build those on the
# cluster and leave them there. metadata.json stays trackable: it is 4 KB of
# provenance, not bulk.
experiments/*/train.npy
experiments/*/train.csv.gz
experiments/*/manifest.jsonl

*.txt
